This IS a real, verified unified diff (generated with `git diff` in the
gitignored target/gecko-src/gecko-dev checkout, branch central-work @
5836a062726f715fda621338a17b51aff30d0a8c) against the upstream file
browser/components/BrowserContentHandler.sys.mjs — apply with `git apply`
or `patch -p1` from the checkout root. Syntax-checked with `node --check`.

Implements pyxis-scheme-and-kiosk-plan.md Part B1 points 1-3 (recognize
`--pyxis-app=<id>`, read PYXIS_APP_ID/PYXIS_DISPLAY_MODE/PYXIS_BACKGROUND
per gecko/src/gecko.rs's compose_launch contract, open a chromeless kiosk
window). See gecko/BUILD_RUNBOOK.md's dated 2026-07-05 kiosk-mode section
for the full design rationale and what is/isn't verified.

UPDATE (2026-07-06, found via a real failed boot, not by inspection): the
flag was originally named plain `--app`. That collides with a flag Gecko's
OWN native startup code already recognizes for a completely different,
pre-existing purpose — browser/app/nsBrowserApp.cpp:167 does
`argc > 1 && IsArg(argv[1], "app")`; if argv[1] is `-app`/`--app`, it treats
argv[2] as a PATH TO AN ALTERNATE application.ini file (an
embedding/XULRunner-style feature), entirely BEFORE XPCOM/JS
initializes — this JS handler never even runs. Invoking
`pyxis-webapp --app testapp` printed "Error: unrecognized path: testapp"
(toolkit/xre/nsAppRunner.cpp:5975) and exited immediately. Renamed to
`--pyxis-app` here (and in gecko/src/gecko.rs's compose_launch and
scripts/create-rootfs.sh's boot invocation) to stop colliding with argv[1]
position-sensitive native parsing. The diff below already reflects this
corrected name throughout (flag parsing, --help text, doc comments) — this
is the current, post-correction state of the file, not the original
kiosk-mode pass.

UPDATE (2026-07-08, final after live QEMU debugging): decoration model is
"GTK owns app-window titlebars; the shell is chromeless". Verified live that
MOZ_GTK_TITLEBAR_DECORATION=none does NOT chromeless a Wayland window (it only
stops Firefox's CSD; GTK still draws its default titlebar -- see the
vela-gtk-titlebar-decoration notes). So app windows keep GTK's own working
titlebar and Evo draws no SSD. The desktop shell (Bloom) is made chromeless
by launching its vela with `--kiosk` (scripts/create-rootfs.sh) -> native
gKioskMode -> gtk_window_set_decorated(false)+gtk_window_fullscreen() at
widget-creation time; Evo composites that fullscreen NON-exclusively
(evo/src/shell/xdg.rs SHELL_APP_ID) so apps stack on top. This diff therefore
does NOT set window.fullScreen/sizemode from the opener callback (that raced
the widget realize and was silently lost); openPyxisAppWindow just opens the
window. See evo-firefox-decoration-arch.

════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
The unified diff below is generated from the checkout and is applied with
  git apply gecko/patches/pyxis/<path>.PYXIS_DIFF
(or `patch -p1 <`). Everything above this line is rationale, not content;
git apply ignores it. Regenerate with scripts/regen-gecko-patches.sh.
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

diff --git a/browser/components/BrowserContentHandler.sys.mjs b/browser/components/BrowserContentHandler.sys.mjs
